    "description": "As part of the Executive Committee of the North Cambridge Artist Association (NOCA), my role is that of Web Developer and Event Planner. \n\nUsing current web technologies, I create and publish web content for 60+ artists, musicians and performers.   I utilize a PHP slideshow to curate current members work. I provide technical web support for all members. \n\nI am also responsible for aspects of social media on Facebook and Twitter.\n\nEach December, with a small team of members, I organize our big holiday Fine Arts Show.  I am responsible for  jurying, publicity, advertising, organizing volunteers, parking logistics, show set-up and break-down.\n\nI have also helped organize NOCA's community participation in at \"Danehy Family Day's\" and \"Cambridge River Festival\".  These are events  allow us to give hands-on art lessons to Cambridge residents of all ages.\n\nI have also served as NOCA liaison to the Cambridge Arts Council (CAC) for Cambridge Open Studio events. The CAC is a non-profit agency that partners with artists, presenters, donors, and audiences,  to provide a vital cultural presence in the region.  ",
